## ML Models (downloaded at runtime)
models/
backend/checkpoints/

## Trained model weights, and anything derived from them, are never committed.
## The checkpoint these were exported from was fitted partly on real mailbox
## corrections. Training on them was defensible — one user's own mail, a model
## serving only that user — but PUBLISHING the result is not: a distributed
## checkpoint is no longer "that specific user's personalized model", and
## Google's restricted-scope terms reach derived and aggregated data as well as
## raw messages. Committing here is publishing, because this repository is
## public. Regenerate locally with `ml/browser/export_onnx.py`; do not commit
## the output. Provenance: docs/ML_PROMOTION_POLICY.md.
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.pkl
ml/browser/artifacts/head.json
ml/browser/artifacts/examples.json
ml/browser/site/head.json
ml/browser/site/examples.json

