## Session working files
# HANDOFF.md is regenerated from live context by the /handoff skill every time
# a session hands over. It is scaffolding for the next session, not a record of
# this repo, and it sat untracked-but-unignored in the root — one `git add -A`
# away from becoming history that would then go stale in place.
/HANDOFF.md

## Stray root install artifacts
# This repo installs per-app — `apps/web` is pnpm (`apps/web/pnpm-lock.yaml`),
# `booklet` is npm — and there is no package.json at the root at all. So a
# root-level `node_modules/` or `package-lock.json` is always the residue of an
# `npm install` run from the wrong directory, and nothing ignored it. Anchored
# with a leading `/` so the tracked `booklet/package-lock.json` is untouched.
/node_modules/
/package-lock.json

## Negative control for the Vercel ignore-build guard.
# scripts/negative_control_ignore_build.mjs writes a deliberately broken copy
# of vercel-ignore-build.sh here and removes it again. It has to live inside
# the repo: the guard resolves its repo root from its own directory, so a copy
# in /tmp would take the "no git checkout here" arm and pass for the wrong
# reason. Ignored so a crashed run cannot leave a committable artifact.
.ignore-build-mutant.sh

## Footage pipeline intermediates.
# `apps/web/scripts/footage/render.sh` records the real UI into PNG frame
# sequences and writes contact sheets and negative-control clips beside them —
# hundreds of megabytes per run, all of it derivable. Only the encoded clips it
# produces are committed, under apps/web/public/footage/. The `.server.log`
# sibling is the captured app's stdout, kept for when a run fails.
apps/web/.footage-frames/
apps/web/.footage-frames.server.log

# Weights & Biases run artifacts. An offline run is a machine-local record of
# a training session, not a dependency manifest, but GitHub reads its frozen
# files/requirements.txt as one — a single stub run accounted for 87 of the
# repo's 93 open Dependabot alerts. Runs belong in the W&B project, not here.
ml/wandb/
